love is a self generating software artifact composed of three
main subprojects
- love: a programming language and runtime written in C
- moon: a C compiler and toolchain written in love
- kore: a coreutils and userland including sh, vi, make, etc.

the love binary artifact is deterministically reproducible
from its source, of which it carries a compressed copy.

;;; we should paste the help below

common invocations
- `love` open a repl
- `love seed` bootstrap from source through local C toolchain
- `love source` lay a source tree
- `love help` `love verbs` more usage info

kore utils can be invoked by symlink
or by passing the name to love as in `love cc`
- cc   (mooncc)
- vi   (chim)
- sh   (lush)
- make (cook)

